Yesterday, you built a semantic search engine using OpenAI embeddings and ChromaDB. Today, you'll turn it into a document intelligence pipeline.
Today's objective: Upload a PDF or DOCX document, extract its text, split it into chunks, generate embeddings, store those chunks in ChromaDB, and retrieve relevant passages using a natural-language question.
This is the foundation of an enterprise RAG (Retrieval-Augmented Generation) platform.

2. Understand RAG architecture
RAG combines two capabilities:
•	Retrieval: Find relevant information from your own documents.
•	Generation: Give that information to an LLM so it can formulate an answer.
For example, imagine an organization has 10,000 employee policy documents. An employee asks:
"What is the company's annual leave policy?"
Instead of sending all 10,000 documents to the LLM, the platform retrieves only the most relevant passages and supplies them as context.
